<p class="note">VERDICT II: no variant beats base-4096 on termination at this horizon — the second negative, and sharper than round I's: with exact token counting base itself terminates only 1/12 (the earlier 6/12 was a words×2 estimate artifact, see README). No variant even improves accuracy; horizon (32k vs 4k) and localization remain the gap to MIT.</p>


<h2>ROUND 2 — MIT'S HORIZON ON OUR SILICON (#1533)</h2>
<p>Rounds I–II ran on CPU at capped horizons because this box's GPU path was dead (#737). It is alive: the whole round now runs on <b>oMLX (Metal GPU)</b> at MIT's full <b>32,768-token</b> think35 protocol — thinking on, temp 0.6 / top_p 0.95 / top_k 20 / <b>presence_penalty 1.5 confirmed applied</b> (seed-fixed probe: pp0 vs pp1.5 outputs differ — the #1506 duplicated-flag class of bug is ruled out on this backend), graded on the last <code>\boxed{}</code> with <code>math-verify</code>. Fixed held-out: 100 MATH-500 + 100 GSM8K-test, selection seed 1533, identical rows for every line. </p>

